64,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at our options, I am concerned about Program C and D. Program C relies on outside providers, which my research shows can take over a year to finalize, and Program D is a joint venture, which often fails.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I share those concerns. Program A reminds me of the call-back trial; it is a noble effort, but if it is not deeply integrated, the benefits may simply vanish once the initial momentum fades.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"I agree with the concerns about Program A and B. Program A would place more pressure on our already vacant ward nursing posts, and Program B relies on physiotherapists, a group we are consistently losing to city posts.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, your analysis of the staff is useful, but look at the finances. Program A and C are off-site, meaning they earn zero regional tariffs. Program B is a capital drain on our shrinking budget for floor space. Program D is the only logical choice.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, you make a strong point about the budget, but I worry about the crowds. Program B and D both bring more people into our rooms and parking, which are already so full by mid-morning. We must be careful not to seize up.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I understand the financial logic, but Program D is a joint venture between midwifery and pediatrics. My findings show that when two departments share a program, it often collapses once the budget or rota becomes a burden.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, you are right to be cautious. If Program D is built on a fragile partnership, it may become another initiative that we quietly bury. We must ensure the structure is permanent, not just a temporary arrangement.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, @Jonathan, while joint ventures are risky, we should consider the actual capacity. My data shows the midwifery rota has unusual slack. Program D utilizes available resources rather than straining the nursing or therapy teams.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, you've just provided the final piece of the puzzle. Program D utilizes existing slack in midwifery and operates on-site, ensuring we actually collect regional tariffs. It is the only option that isn't a financial or operational liability.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, @Misaki, it is heartening that the midwifery team has some room to breathe. However, I still worry about our poor parking and the shuttle. If Program D brings many new parents in, will they find a place to park?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, I understand your worry, but we must weigh it against the risk of total collapse. Program D's use of existing slack is a strong point, provided we can clearly define who holds the budget.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, I agree. If we can establish a clear, enduring structure for Program D, it avoids the pitfalls of the other options. It seems the most likely to survive without becoming another forgotten attempt.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, parking is a challenge, but it is a manageable one compared to the risk of staff burnout or total program failure. Program D is the only option that doesn't deepen our current staffing crises.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, parking is a triviality compared to insolvency. We are facing a shrinking budget and a need for revenue. Program D is the only candidate that aligns with our financial constraints and staffing reality. The logic is absolute.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, you are always so certain, and I admire your strength. But for a new mother with a little one, a full car park is not a triviality; it is a great stress. Still, I see we are all leaning toward Program D.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree. While the joint nature of Program D is a risk, the other options present even greater dangers to our stability and staff. If we are clear about ownership, it is our best path. I vote for Program D.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. While I remain mindful of the fragility of new initiatives, Program D avoids the systemic risks of the others and utilizes existing capacity. I vote for Program D.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Program D is the only choice that respects our current staffing limits and utilizes available slack without risking further burnout. I vote for Program D.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Shion,,The logic is inescapable. Program D is the only option that generates on-site revenue while avoiding the staffing crises and capital drains of the others. I vote for Program D.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit sad to think of the stress our new parents might face in the car park, but I cannot ignore the kindness you have all shown in considering our staff. I shall trust your wisdom. I vote for Program D.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
